Plugin I/O: what a ported shell plugin needs to talk to the system.

- process.spawn(cmd, args, {env, cwd, stdout, stderr}) for long-running
  children read line by line. The child leads its own process group, which is
  SIGKILLed when the owning view, plugin or runtime goes away. run() takes
  {env, cwd} too. Children still start from an empty environment: granted host
  variables (Capabilities::process_env) are copied in, and only those names may
  be set explicitly. cwd must be absolute and inside a read root.
- net.connect({path}) for granted unix sockets (Capabilities::network_unix),
  and reads without the 30 s idle timeout, on a dedicated thread instead of the
  shared background pool.
- fetch: binary bodies (arrayBuffer()), a timeout option, and stream: true.
- image()/AvatarImage.new() take a path or raster bytes. A URL string used to
  make GPUI fetch around the network grant and is now refused; a relative path
  resolves under Capabilities::asset_root and an absolute one must be in a read
  root.

